-- KAN-462. A brand carries one type set in every branch (KAN-480).
--
-- The NorteShopping and Via Catarina rulings (decisions.md, 2026-11-11/12)
-- corrected these brands' mall units; this applies the same set to every
-- other branch we serve, so a user tagging a task reaches all of them or
-- none. The owner asked for it here rather than in a separate ticket
-- (2026-11-12), which is why KAN-501 is closed unworked.
--
--   Flying Tiger Copenhagen   store + gift          (was discount_store x70, florist x2)
--   Zara Home                 store + home          (was clothing AND home)
--   OTRO Perfume Concept      store + beauty        (was spa x3)
--   Twinset                   store + womens_clothing
--   Teresinha Carteiras       store + handbag       (was clothing)
--   Naco                      beauty_salon + nail_salon  (was spa)
--   Chocolate Rosa            bakery                (was tea)
--
-- Left alone on purpose: `MAC` in Almada is a historical landmark, not the
-- cosmetics brand (every `MAC Cosmetics` row is already store + beauty);
-- `Twin Set Spa`, `Teresinha Bijuteria/Cabeleireiros/Lingerie` and the `Naco`
-- restaurants and cinema are other businesses sharing a word; `ORIENTAL` is
-- a generic name, not a brand.
--
-- The same decision is recorded for each Overture id in
-- src/overtureCandidateOverrides.json (batch `kan462_brand_type_sets`), so a
-- refresh that re-decides a row keeps this set. One Flying Tiger id moved
-- there from `reviewed_discount_store`.
--
-- Retypes only: no row is added or removed. Idempotent.
